    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I’ve always seen mathematics as a tool for understanding patterns and structure in the world, especially in biology and philosophy. As a PhD student, I use it pragmatically—like modeling ecosystems or analyzing data—but I don’t find it inherently beautiful or intuitive. It’s precise, sometimes cold, and I appreciate its logic, though I prefer deeper questions about meaning and ethics.",
